  "rationale": "After 100 evaluations (56 pipelined + 44 pipelined_m), only pipelined has produced feasible designs (25 feasible, best area 39336 um2). pipelined_m has 0 feasible designs in 44 evals, likely because its reduced register count does not improve area enough to matter, or its latency/throughput characteristics don't help. iterative and unrolled_k (other members) also have 0 feasible designs, confirming that only pipelined architectures meet the 32 MSps throughput and 0.5 us batch latency constraints. The 11 designs on the merged front are all from pipelined. With 100 evaluations remaining (round 2 of 4), I should focus entirely on refining the pipelined front: the current feasible region is data_width 14-20, n_iter 12-18. The key trade-off is area vs accuracy_bits. I narrow the ranges to focus the search: data_width 14-20 (below 14 likely fails accuracy, above 20 adds area without accuracy benefit since max_abs_err constraint is 2^-12), n_iter 12-18 (below 12 likely fails accuracy, above 18 adds area), angle_guard 0-2 and frac_guard 0-2 (small guards to minimize area while maintaining accuracy), rounding both options. This refinement should tighten the Pareto front and identify the minimum-area feasible design for the selection rule (min area_um2)."
